WEBVTT

00:00.390 --> 00:03.800
Let's say you've always wanted to automate
the work you keep putting off.

00:03.850 --> 00:07.800
Issuing refunds, answering tickets,
or even updating every order.

00:07.980 --> 00:10.250
But one wrong call can't be undone.

00:10.300 --> 00:11.570
Introducing Rehearsal.

00:11.660 --> 00:15.600
Your agent works on a private copy first,
and shows you every change.

00:15.900 --> 00:18.600
It runs on the MCP server Synapse builds,

00:18.700 --> 00:21.600
with Claude, Cursor, or any agent you like.

00:21.700 --> 00:23.800
One command, and it's protected.

00:24.000 --> 00:26.800
Another app? Rehearsal init sets it up.

00:27.300 --> 00:30.450
And when something looks wrong,
it stops and asks you first.

00:30.550 --> 00:34.350
Look closer. Actions, changes,
customers, or sources.

00:34.450 --> 00:38.750
Say yes, and the same steps replay on live,
checked row by row.

00:38.800 --> 00:40.700
Every reviewer gets their own link.

00:40.750 --> 00:43.600
Every agent action, rehearsed first.

00:44.200 --> 00:46.150
Nothing goes live until you say yes.

00:46.250 --> 00:47.600
Rehearsal.
